                "summary": "Controller and preview logic are sound: switchCamera states, the cameraAskedAt guard, change only on effect, problemLine for the back camera only, and the old camera's late answer/ended are all guarded by camera===own, and createPreview stays backward compatible. Changes required: (1) the tests do not guard that the view's key is separate from teaching's. Setting RECOGNISE_FACING_KEY to amysecho-camera-facing in dist still passes all 51 tests in recognise+app. (2) The hidden switch breaks the NG-48 focus guarantee. cameraButton is not in focusable, so when it is focused and hidden by a redraw (recording timer ends, giving confirm/unknown/unusable) focus drops to the page (recognise.ts:794-795,809,914-920). (3) Docs and comments still say the gesture view always uses the front camera with its picture: docs/capture.md:113-120, docs/recognise.md:18-19 and :104, src/capture/capture.ts:17-19.",
